    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\nMan Buys New Chevrolet Corvette Z06 Convertible for $170,460, Drives 843 Miles, Sells for $129,000\n22 photos\nPhoto: Bring a Trailer\nEven though I’ll be the first to tell you that the absolute sweet spot for a used C8 Z06, as far as the buyer is concerned, is that early six-figure mark... if you can get yours for around $105,000, it’s about as good as it gets. And yet, I absolutely love what I’m seeing here. It’s more or less my ideal Z06 spec, for what it’s worth.\nLet’s focus on that word for a second. Worth . Because what I’ve done just now is I’ve gone on Chevrolet’s official configurator to build myself a brand-new 2027 Z06 Convertible with the exact same spec as this one, and guess what? You’d be spending roughly $180,000. So, I’m inclined to almost call this a steal.\nThe person who just landed this car at auction, did so for $129,000, plus a buyer’s fee – and this thing is basically still brand-new with just 843 miles on the clock. The original MSRP was $170,460. The seller took the hit, which was unavoidable.\nLook, the economics of buying a used Z06 for over $130k+ are complex. That’s what this car cost when factoring in the buyer’s fee. But this also isn’t any regular Z06. It’s a 3LZ Convertible, with the Z07 performance suspension and carbon-ceramic Brembo brakes (courtesy of the Z06 Ultimate Performance package), but also the Visible Carbon Fiber Aero Package and the Carbon Fiber Interior Trim Level 2 Package.\nAside from the power-retractable hardtop, other exterior highlights include the several carbon fiber elements (splitter, rocker, high-wing spoiler, dive planes), as well as the black-finished 20” and 21” forged wheels with Michelin Pilot Sport Cup 2R tires. There’s also a front-axle lift system with memory settings, and you get Magnetic Selective Ride Control.\nMeanwhile, inside is where you’ll find the heated and ventilated GT2 bucket seats in Jet Black leather and with Adrenaline Red stitching. Also the microsuede upper trim, a performance data and video recorder, carpeted floor mats, dual-zone automatic climate control, cruise control, a head-up display, a 14-speaker Bose sound system, plus several electronic driver aids such as rear cross-traffic alert, lane-keep assist, side blind-zone alert, and forward collision alert.\nPhoto: Bring a Trailer As for performance, we’re dealing with a mid-mounted 5.5-liter LT6 V8 , good for 670 horsepower and 460 lb-ft of torque. Everything gets sent to the rear wheels via an eight-speed dual-clutch automatic transmission.\nWith the help of a 1-foot rollout, the Z06 can rocket to 60 mph (97 kph) in just 2.6 seconds. The top speed is 195 mph (314 kph), although the Z07 package can push that number down to 189 mph (304 kph).\nUltimately, I genuinely think this car was well-bought. Just a few weeks ago we saw this 2024 Z06 Convertible go for $122,000, and it had 13k miles on the clock – which is really far from delivery miles. But what do you guys think?\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nchevrolet corvette z06 convertible Chevrolet Corvette Z06 corvette z06 Corvette Chevrolet Chevrolet Corvette auction used cars\nAbout the author: Sergiu Tudose\nSergiu got to experience both American and European car \"scenes\" at an early age (his father drove a Ford Fiesta XR2 supermini in the 80s). After spending over 15 years at local and international auto publications, he's starting to appreciate comfort behind the wheel more than raw power and acceleration. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1970 Plymouth Satellite Springs Back to Life After 36 Years at a Farm; Too Many Doors?",
